// (something like vendor.camerad.source@1), which nervus.camerad converts into this interface. That way:
//   - standard semantics (facing=front) are declared by the platform, and vendors can't crown themselves;
//   - vendors can have any private capability (structured light, ToF depth) through their own interface, without polluting the standard;
//   - the data plane still goes direct: nervus.camerad hands the vendor's TransferHandle on to the App,
//     and frames aren't copied once more through camerad.
